[53.1440, "o", "\r\n"]
[53.2596, "o", "**shop/discounts.py**  \r\n"]
[54.7047, "o", "- **Issue:** Line 20 calculates the BULK discount incorrectly. It returns `int(total * RATES[code])`, which gives the discount amount (15 % of total) instead of the discounted total. For consistency with the TENOFF case, it should be `int(total * (1 - RATES[code]))`. This causes the BULK code to reduce the price to only 15 % of the original rather than 85 %.\r\n\r\n"]
[55.1530, "o", "**shop/tax.py**  \r\n"]
[56.3907, "o", "- **Issue:** Lines 4‑5 use floating‑point arithmetic (`cents * (1 + RATE)`) for monetary calculations, which can introduce rounding errors due to binary floating‑point representation. For accurate cents‑based math, use integer arithmetic (e.g., `(cents * 10825 + 5000) // 10000`) or the `Decimal` type.\r\n"]
[56.3948, "o", "\r\n✓ 1 delegation · 44s · ↑14.9k ↓2.7k · ctx 2%\r\n\r\n"]
